{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554076-tremere-timeline","id":1554076,"title":"Tremere timeline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-01T03:42:10-07:00","id":1554076,"title":"Tremere timeline","content":"I'm wondering about the eldest Tremere possible.<br /> <br /> It seems that before they crashed the Diamond and got themselves recognised as an Order they were likely something of a nameless order for a few hundred years.<br /> <br /> Some time c400 they free a God-monster that becomes their 7th Watchtower. And after that you can have Hollowed Tremere as we know them today (though maybe they are unlikely to have survived this long).<br /> <br /> Were they immortal before that? Vampire Ancient Mysteries talks about Breath stealers, but I'm unclear in whether they were Immortal and whether any survived? Or were the five who were transformed by the 7th Watchtower? Were earlier Tremere mortal awakened monster hunters?<br /> <br /> Could they have been stealing souls before that go conquer death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-01T07:41:46-07:00","id":1554080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554076-tremere-timeline#post1554076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Were they immortal before that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's not out of the question that some earlier Tremere would have experimented with lichdom as a means of exploring their ideals of supremacy, although perhaps not intrinsically and without argument from some of them. While some specific tenets of common Moros beliefs about the natural progression of death seem liable to be dismissed as lies of the Five Dragons, I could see some extending their philosophy to an idea that mortality imposes a pressure to aggressively pursue imperium.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could they have been stealing souls before that go conquer death?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Reaping is not exactly a necessary method towards immortality, and even kind of an inefficient one compared to other options. That was always one of the big criticisms of the Tremere as they appeared in the First Edition core; even allowing for an origin that was imposed upon them, the sales pitch seemed pretty weak. That's part of why Left-Hand Path expanded them.<br /> <br /> And I think even with their current write-up, people get a bit too hung up on the immortality, when my read of their tenets make it almost incidental to their concerns or motivations.<br /> <br /> What I would say is that I think there certainly would have been Tremere invested in Reaping before they had those with Hollow. Perhaps not intrinsically; I could see the modern Tremere being a lot more invested in taking souls for the sake of their studies because the way their powers facilitate it and their condition necessitates it selects a lot more for that as the common approach. Whereas I think that before that, you could get more of them who'd want to study it less invasively, even if it is a common Obsession amongst them. Either way, it's still more in the interests of understanding its secrets and why exactly humans are so uniquely positioned to Awaken and Ascend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-01T12:31:53-07:00","id":1554086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554076-tremere-timeline#post1554076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire Ancient Mysteries talks about Breath stealers, but I'm unclear in whether they were Immortal and whether any survived? Or were the five who were transformed by the 7th Watchtower?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Ancient Mysteries</i> predates any of the Tremere rewrites, and it's not clear that they're even talking about the Tremere. That link only seems to appears later when <i>Left-Hand Path</i> refers to the Tremere as being turned into 'Breath-eaters' by some monster kindred called the Theban during the 'Theban Captivity' (additionally, there's a sidebar on pg.80 that says that the write-up is deliberately written with a bunch of offhand references to <i>Requiem</i>...<br /> <br /> With 2e, the Breath-eater stuff seems to be written out. Maybe. The 'Theban Captivity' is now just the 'Captivity' which seems to be multiple different things that happened at once, and could still include the Theban Captivity... Except that the timeline from <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> says that the Theban essentially dominated the Tremere whilst they were already enduring the Captivity, so the Theban can't have been the being who inflicted the Captivity condition on the Tremere... (at least probably not). Then again, the timeline is a bit odd and not without inconsistencies.<br /> <br /> Basically, as I see it, the write-up in <i>LHP</i> has been partially retconned, but a lot of it could still stand if you wanted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could they have been stealing souls before that go conquer death? </div> </div> </div>I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Isator Levi</a> , the 2e Tremere don't seem all that bothered by death. Like, I'm sure they don't mind living forever, but it's not really the point of the Order in the way it was for the original legacy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-01T17:50:28-07:00","id":1554093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554076-tremere-timeline?p=1554086#post1554086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Ancient Mysteries</i> predates any of the Tremere rewrites, and it's not clear that they're even talking about the Tremere. That link only seems to appears later when <i>Left-Hand Path</i> refers to the Tremere as being turned into 'Breath-eaters' by some monster kindred called the Theban during the 'Theban Captivity' (additionally, there's a sidebar on pg.80 that says that the write-up is deliberately written with a bunch of offhand references to <i>Requiem</i>...<br /> <br /> With 2e, the Breath-eater stuff seems to be written out. Maybe. The 'Theban Captivity' is now just the 'Captivity' which seems to be multiple different things that happened at once, and could still include the Theban Captivity... Except that the timeline from <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> says that the Theban essentially dominated the Tremere whilst they were already enduring the Captivity, so the Theban can't have been the being who inflicted the Captivity condition on the Tremere... (at least probably not). Then again, the timeline is a bit odd and not without inconsistencies.<br /> <br /> Basically, as I see it, the write-up in <i>LHP</i> has been partially retconned, but a lot of it could still stand if you wanted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Isator Levi</a> , the 2e Tremere don't seem all that bothered by death. Like, I'm sure they don't mind living forever, but it's not really the point of the Order in the way it was for the original legacy.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't remember where I read it, but there was a clear reference to the Sundered World Dark Era, and stealing the hearts of Pangeans to make Demenses, which suggests that the 'original' Tremere were hunting monsters before and just kept some of what they were doing secret...<br /> <br /> But then something reacted poorly, their Captivity changed them. I find it appealing to have a Breath-Eaters phase where they had not yet adjusted to their condition...<br /> <br /> And then later they escape the captivity and become Modern Tremere (and maybe eventually Hunt down and kill all the remaining Breath-Eaters...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  grammar 10-01-2025, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-02T05:41:51-07:00","id":1554099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554076-tremere-timeline?p=1554093#post1554093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't remember where I read it, but there was a clear reference to the Sundered World Dark Era, and stealing the hearts of Pangeans to make Demenses, which suggests that the 'original' Tremere were hunting monsters before and just kept some of what they were doing secret...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in Tome of the Pentacle, yeah.<br /> <br /> Mind, considering that there's a span of about six thousand years between the Sundering and the appearance of the formally named Tremere, I think the intention there is somewhat of them being very distant spiritual successors of the premise, rather than there being a direct continuity of power through monster hunting that stretches back so far.<br /> <br /> I would note that stealing souls is not the only method that mages have for draining something vital out of people. There's a proposition that part of the nature of the Captivity is that the Tremere could not replenish mana without the approval of their masters, so it could be that they became dependent on spells preying on other humans in a manner similar to monsters. It adds a transitional phase to the requirements that will come of Hollow, but isn't quite as on the nose, and maybe gets a bit more focused on why they consolidate a belief in the magical symbolism of hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 10-02-2025, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-02T08:19:32-07:00","id":1554103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mind, considering that there's a span of about six thousand years between the Sundering and the appearance of the formally named Tremere, I think the intention there is somewhat of them being very distant spiritual successors of the premise, rather than there being a direct continuity of power through monster hunting that stretches back so far. </div> </div> </div>I entirely agree, in principle it is vague enough that you could not count the Dark Eras stuff as canon and rewrite their past at your own table... But it is clear there is intended to be some kind of precursor...<br /> <br /> And then someone pointed me at To the Strongest, and it is such a let down. Though from that we get the Tremere at the time didn't steal souls, and allegedly keep customs from before the Fall - and that they have fluency in high speech... More mention of an Ancient Vampire in Egypt. And now I want too read this from the Vampire's perspective...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-02T13:20:14-07:00","id":1554108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554076-tremere-timeline?p=1554103#post1554103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then someone pointed me at To the Strongest, and it is such a let down.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that <i>TtS</i> was written after <i>Left-Hand Path</i> and about 3 years before <i>Nameless &amp; Accursed</i>.<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that the <i>2e </i>core doesn't really mention any of the changes that were coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-03T10:07:06-07:00","id":1554122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554076-tremere-timeline?p=1554103#post1554103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I entirely agree, in principle it is vague enough that you could not count the Dark Eras stuff as canon and rewrite their past at your own table... But it is clear there is intended to be some kind of precursor...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying the stuff in The Sundered World is not canon.<br /> <br /> I'm saying that a direct line of descent over six thousand years and stretching back into the literal Stone Age is absurd.<br /> <br /> Like, there can be an enduring tradition of understanding that murdering Pangeans was a thing that was done, and when the Tremere come together they say &quot;those were the ancestors of our tradition&quot;.<br /> <br /> It is about as literal and credible as Rome having been founded by some demigod who could lend the city his name. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then someone pointed me at To the Strongest, and it is such a let down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you expect the thing focused on the origins of the Hellenistic Mediterranean to include references to a group that had been established to have origins in northern and eastern Europe?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-03T12:20:54-07:00","id":1554126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554076-tremere-timeline?p=1554122#post1554122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you expect the thing focused on the origins of the Hellenistic Mediterranean to include references to a group that had been established to have origins in northern and eastern Europe?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I heard people say &quot;oh the Order began with Alexander&quot; and recommend the dark era, and then read some cool proto-Order type stuff which is really good.<br /> <br /> So the side bar which does mention the Tremere in passing was sa rather large let down.<br /> <br /> No, I'm not saying it should have been something else, but A) I didn't know the Tremere's origin were Northern and Eastern Europe, and B) the didn't originate around the time of Alexander in any meaningful sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm saying that a direct line of descent over six thousand years and stretching back into the literal Stone Age is absurd. </div> </div> </div>Given how Mage works, you could easily imagine a lost history where this isn't absurd, with Liches passing down a philosophy go each succeeding generation, or Daimonomikons from the Time Before inducting new Mages into a secret cult dedicated to dominating monsters...<br /> <br /> Even if it mutated several times.<br /> <br /> But having asked the question, I have found that the Tremere weren't Liches at all until much later, and that linking them to 6000 year old Deicide is tenuous at best.<br /> <br /> In fact, I think the Tremere claim the originate from Atlantis, at least by some accounts (1st edition certainly suggests it, and I'm not sure anything in 2nd contradicts that).<br /> <br /> The worship of a Bound God is kinda interesting, especially if they join by feeding the souls to the Abyss to become Hollow - but I haven't read the 2e Hollow initiation stuff recently - asking &quot;what are the consequences of feeding souls to an Abyssal God monster?&quot; is an exercise left to your table.<br /> <br /> But I'm still curious about the ancient Vampire sorcerer (&quot;the Theban&quot;), the Captivity, and the Breath-Eaters (which if they dissapeared 900 years ago from Kindred records, were they huntted down and destoryed by the Tremere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-03T19:43:56-07:00","id":1554134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554076-tremere-timeline?p=1554126#post1554126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm not saying it should have been something else, but A) I didn't know the Tremere's origin were Northern and Eastern Europe, and B) the didn't originate around the time of Alexander in any meaningful sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ora, people are saying <i>the Orders</i> \u2014 the first Sect that was the proto-Diamond \u2014 got their starting point in the time of Alexander.<br /> <br /> Because the groups that would cohere into the Diamond started to form around that time when the Great Cults were the main big games on the globe before then.<br /> <br /> The Tremere were a Nameless Order before they joined the Diamond, a process which is described in different levels of detail in Nameless and Accursed and Tome of the Pentacle. They are deliberately obscure, because they are a weird antagonist faction that does not have the numbers or broad metaphysical backing of the Seers or the Scelesti. Their timeline is not filled in because, like much of the setting, it is a secret history in a world where time travel (and, more notably, massive unpredictable retroactive alterations to reality from poking fundamental forces) exists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But having asked the question, I have found that the Tremere weren't Liches at all until much later, and that linking them to 6000 year old Deicide is tenuous at best. </div> </div> </div>Approximately as tenuous as linking the Cainite Heresy in Hunter to the Longinian heresy of the same name in Requiem for Rome, and yet there is a whole section in Night Stalkers going over the facts of how an ill-advised Gnostic/Manichean heresy has managed to transform across the centuries to the point where its signature question has lost its answer \u2014 the first eleven words of the section are &quot;Heresies don't survive 1600 years. That's not how human society works.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, I think the Tremere claim the originate from Atlantis, at least by some accounts (1st edition certainly suggests it, and I'm not sure anything in 2nd contradicts that). </div> </div> </div>The Tremere claim all sorts of stuff. That doesn't mean they believe any of it, as is evident from the explicit statement in their Nameless and Accursed writeup that they deliberately sow lies and misdirection about their own history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The worship of a Bound God is kinda interesting, especially if they join by feeding the souls to the Abyss to become Hollow - but I haven't read the 2e Hollow initiation stuff recently - asking &quot;what are the consequences of feeding souls to an Abyssal God monster?&quot; is an exercise left to your table. </div> </div> </div>Cost of doing business. The Seventh Dragon is the universal hunger (not of the Abyss despite being in the Abyss) that lets them continue to meddle with souls at a particularly high level as an institution. You might link this to Ammut from Mummy if you were so inclined, but any agenda you could come up with would be an invention tailored to your own chronicle, because as far as the books are making declarative statements they're just saying that the consequences are the continued existence and propagation of the Tremere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I'm still curious about the ancient Vampire sorcerer (&quot;the Theban&quot;), the Captivity, and the Breath-Eaters (which if they dissapeared 900 years ago from Kindred records, were they huntted down and destoryed by the Tremere? </div> </div> </div>See &quot;the Tremere's history is deliberately obscure and they have diegetically made it moreso over time.&quot;<br /> <br /> They're fascist-coded human-supremacists who think giving up their own souls to the hunger of the cosmic oversoul entitles them to do whatever they please in the pursuit of ultimate power. You are not going to find a straight answer to what happened in the Captivity if they have anything to say about it, and that goes double in an edition where they are no longer simply linked to one monstrous splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-04T04:27:00-07:00","id":1554141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554076-tremere-timeline?p=1554126#post1554126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But having asked the question, I have found that the Tremere weren't Liches at all until much later, and that linking them to 6000 year old Deicide is tenuous at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how literal you want to be, <i>N&amp;A</i> and <i>TotP</i> actually does potentially elaborate on this a little. Like, both have the same basic premise, that the Tremere are aware dimly of what the Vinca mages were up to with regards the Pangaeans. However, from <i>The Sundered World</i>, we know exactly why the Vinca did what they did; it was for practical purposes of keeping their society together. Therefore, we know the Tremere are actually kinda wrong in their mythologising of these events as some promethean act of 'breaking the gods'.<br /> <br /> Except, <i>TotP</i> actually elaborates that the Tremere during the time they were with the Diamond are aware of this inconsistency. They basically claim that their beliefs are merely prefigured by the Vinca; they &quot;followed \u2014 however unknowingly \u2014 the universal principles of hunger and passion&quot;.<br /> <br /> <i>N&amp;A</i> has none of that nuance. Now, that's probably the result of it simply being an earlier book, but it does leave an interesting picture where we can actually see the Tremere simplifying their own history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, I think the Tremere claim the originate from Atlantis, at least by some accounts (1st edition certainly suggests it, and I'm not sure anything in 2nd contradicts that). </div> </div> </div>Basically everything contradicts it. Like, the story of 77 generations of Tremere in <i>LHP</i> has been moved from Atlantis to actual history, and the etymology of 'Tremere' is different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I'm still curious about the ancient Vampire sorcerer (&quot;the Theban&quot;), the Captivity, and the Breath-Eaters (which if they dissapeared 900 years ago from Kindred records, were they huntted down and destoryed by the Tremere? </div> </div> </div>Personally, I wonder about creating a new group that makes use of this older material. I dunno, 'Theban' mages?<br /> <br /> Like, I really like the 2e version of the Tremere, but at this point there's very little left of the original concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-04T06:04:16-07:00","id":1554142,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">You could even have some Pentacle traditions have started with the Tremere. The Slayers from <i>Summoners</i>, trained to be highly effective at combating summoned beings, for example, could be one. By more easily producing Supernal Anchors (artificial souls stones) through binding summons into vessels, then spare a mage's potential Gnosis. It also allows them to delve in more dangerous summoning work, confident that they can deal with the most dangerous entities.<br /> <br /> I imagine the old research of the Tremere holds many useful discoveries. Their goal of pushing the boundaries of magic and their ruthless ambition means they investigated Mysteries in ways less hubristic mages would not have considered.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T03:34:25-07:00","id":1554154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554076-tremere-timeline?p=1554142#post1554142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By more easily producing Supernal Anchors...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Supernal Anchor merit itself would be a pretty good candidate for a Tremere invention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T07:47:59-07:00","id":1554157,"title":"","content":"Wow, just read the Supernal Anchor merit, and I hate it.<br /> <br /> Pretty easy to convert to 2e, but no.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T12:31:30-07:00","id":1554166,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're fascist-coded human-supremacists who think giving up their own souls to the hunger of the cosmic oversoul entitles them to do whatever they please in the pursuit of ultimate power. You are not going to find a straight answer to what happened in the Captivity if they have anything to say about it, and that goes double in an edition where they are no longer simply linked to one monstrous splat. </div> </div> </div>Except ironically the Prometheans and bound aren't on the hit list because they already are soulless and make the Tremere uncomfortable to be around.<br /> <br /> Also, for their history, it's very suspicious how a group so obsessed with the number 7, was lucky/unlucky enough for everything to go wrong when they hit 77 generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-09T11:31:25-07:00","id":1554269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554076-tremere-timeline?p=1554141#post1554141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the etymology of 'Tremere' is different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. Left-Hand Path says &quot;he who shakes the boundaries&quot;, Nameless and Accursed says &quot;shakers of the borders&quot;, Tome of the Pentacle has a few references that invoke the old meaning (which is really hardly much different than the new), and they're both pretty indirect or poetic translations of the Latin verb &quot;tremere&quot; in any case. I think the essence is pretty much the same, the only difference is that Second Edition doesn't explicitly make out that there's a longer term that it could be derived from (although it doesn't specifically exclude it), or attributes it as a Shadow Name to a legendary founder.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}